rawtrp_demos — first-party Rust port of the RawTherapee demosaic kernels
=========================================================================

The demosaicing algorithms in this crate are **ports of RawTherapee**, which is
licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0. This project (fot-lab/fotlab)
is likewise licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0, so the port is
licence-compatible.

Upstream project:  RawTherapee  <https://www.rawtherapee.com/>
Upstream licence:  GNU General Public License v3.0
Upstream source:   external/RawTherapee (git submodule, pinned)

Provenance
----------
Each ported file carries a header naming the upstream source file it was ported
from, e.g.

    Ported from external/RawTherapee/rtengine/vng4_demosaic_RT.cc

and reproduces the upstream copyright line(s) of that file. The upstream sources
are used read-only: this repository never modifies them and never ships a
`.patch` against them (rules/DESIGN/detail/FOTLAB-NATIVE-000004.md C1).

Ported files and their upstream origin
--------------------------------------
  src/bayer/bilinear.rs   <- rtengine/bayer_bilinear_demosaic.cc   (c) 2020 Ingo Weyrich
  src/bayer/vng4.rs       <- rtengine/vng4_demosaic_RT.cc          (c) Ingo Weyrich
  ...                    (see each file's header for the exact origin)

Shared helpers reproduce small pieces of rtengine infrastructure that the
kernels depend on, with the upstream file named in each header:

  src/cfa.rs     <- rtengine/rawimage.h  (FC / ISGREEN / ISBLUE / prefilters)
  src/array2d.rs <- rtengine/array2D.h   (array2D<T>)
  src/math.rs    <- rtengine/rt_math.h   (intp / min / max / LIM / CLIP / SGN)
  src/border.rs  <- rtengine/demosaic_algos.cc  (RawImageSource::border_interpolate)

